body.text:
BonfyreStitch's legacy reconstruction model is powerful but node_hash/cache identity alone is not enough for the mature machine. A realization can be byte/content-addressed and still be invalid under changed authority, toolchain, information policy, economics, proof requirements, latent calibration or external freshness.

Converge Stitch/current materializer with DerivationRef/RepresentationRef/ValidityVector/EvidenceLocality:
- semantic identity and derivation identity stay separate from body/cache identity;
- cached body reuse requires the relevant validity coordinates to still match;
- source/toolchain delta may invalidate body without rewriting canonical semantic state;
- price/rate change should update economics without rebuilding unrelated content bodies;
- external freshness expiry invalidates only dependent observations/derivations;
- LOCAL_ONLY proof cannot become canonical release because a compiled artifact exists;
- generated/compiled realization is replaceable and non-authoritative.

Prove selective invalidation with at least two mutations: one that should force rematerialization (operator/toolchain/semantic dependency change) and one that should only recompute economics/query projection while reusing the same body.
